   $q$Why does the author describe the swan, the kingfisher and the egret struggling during the drought?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the other birds were never really talented at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated"},{"text":"To explain why Tamsin first began measuring the other birds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"To show that the strengths Tamsin envied do not help now, while hers do.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To prove that the marsh will never recover from the dry summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that the strengths Tamsin envied do not help now, while hers do.$q$, $q$The drought makes floating, diving and the egret's skills useless, while Tamsin's long legs and stillness succeed. The other birds still have their talents; the drought simply changes which strengths matter.$q$, 'draft', '05118b28-a66c-5255-ad20-ee042c6532b9')
