   $q$Which statement best expresses a theme of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Moving to a new country means forgetting the past.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Old radios are more valuable than any modern technology.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Songs and stories shared across generations keep memories alive.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Children should never choose games over listening to adults.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Songs and stories shared across generations keep memories alive.$q$, $q$The grandfather passes his mother's songs to the speaker, who learns and hums them too. The poem shows the past being kept, not forgotten, after the move across the ocean.$q$, 'draft', 'eb35e28f-3ccf-550f-893c-d60177290a2e')
