-- Passage rg7-word-parts-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('12004cef-d6f1-59ec-9cfd-ca9516613eb8', 'rg7-word-parts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Benefit Concert$q$, $q$The roof of the Lakeview Community Center had leaked for two winters. When the director said there was no money to fix it, Amara Okafor had an idea. Her family's band could hold a benefit concert, and every ticket sold would go toward a new roof.

Amara's grandfather, who had played trumpet for fifty years, agreed to help. He called a retired music teacher named Mr. Lindqvist, who became the concert's main benefactor. Mr. Lindqvist paid for the posters and the folding chairs, and he asked for nothing in return.

On the night of the show, the gym was packed. The audience clapped along to every song, and the youngest children danced near the stage. During the last number, a speaker crackled and the bass guitar became barely audible. Amara's cousin Tomas quickly swapped a cable, and the sound came roaring back.

After the concert, a line formed near the stage. People wanted the band members to autograph their programs, which made Amara laugh. She had never signed her name for a fan before.

The next morning, the director counted the money. The concert had raised enough to replace the roof, with a little left over for new lights. Amara's grandfather said the best part was not the money. It was seeing the whole neighborhood fill one room for the same reason.$q$, 'draft')
