   $q$The Latin root bene means "good" or "well." What is a "benefit concert" in this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A concert held outdoors on a warm summer night","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A concert performed only by beginning musicians","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A concert that anyone can attend without paying","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A concert held to raise money for a good cause","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A concert held to raise money for a good cause$q$, $q$Bene means "good," and the passage says every ticket sold would go toward a new roof, so the concert helps a good cause. The concert was not free, since tickets were sold.$q$, 'draft', '12004cef-d6f1-59ec-9cfd-ca9516613eb8')
