   $q$The root aud means "hear," and the suffix -ible means "able to be." What does it mean that the bass guitar became "barely audible"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It could hardly be heard by the people in the gym","is_correct":true},{"text":"It became much too loud for the small children","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It broke apart and could never be played again","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It could hardly be seen from the back of the gym","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It could hardly be heard by the people in the gym$q$, $q$Audible means "able to be heard," so barely audible means the sound was very faint. The guitar did not break for good, because the passage says the sound came roaring back after Tomas swapped a cable.$q$, 'draft', '12004cef-d6f1-59ec-9cfd-ca9516613eb8')
