   $q$The prefix pre- means "before," and the Latin root dict means "say." What does "predict" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To tell ahead of time what is likely to happen","is_correct":true},{"text":"To measure the exact size of the volcano","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"To explain why something happened afterward","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"To stop something dangerous from happening","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To tell ahead of time what is likely to happen$q$, $q$Pre plus dict means "say before," so scientists use the patterns to tell in advance when danger is growing. To stop something would be to prevent it, but the passage describes scientists giving warnings, not stopping eruptions.$q$, 'draft', 'bb8241f0-37f6-5ff9-8156-bf2bbffe9f5a')
