   $q$The prefix dis- means "apart," and rupt means "break." What does it mean that volcanoes can "disrupt daily life"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They can break up people's normal routines","is_correct":true},{"text":"They can make people's routines much easier","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They can help people repair roads and crops","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They can slowly change people's habits over centuries","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They can break up people's normal routines$q$, $q$Dis plus rupt means "break apart," and the passage gives examples of canceled flights and ash covering roads. Nothing in the text suggests the change is slow or takes centuries.$q$, 'draft', 'bb8241f0-37f6-5ff9-8156-bf2bbffe9f5a')
