   $q$The prefix pro- means "forward," and the Latin root ject means "throw." What does it mean that Priya "projected her voice"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She lowered her voice to a soft whisper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She recorded her voice to play back later","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"She sent her voice out strongly so it carried far","is_correct":true},{"text":"She changed her voice to sound like the coach","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She sent her voice out strongly so it carried far$q$, $q$Pro plus ject means "throw forward," and the passage says she spoke so that players at the far end of the huddle could hear. A whisper would do the opposite.$q$, 'draft', 'fc1b71d7-429d-5bf8-8214-cd5d24f0039d')
