   $q$The prefix re- means "back," and ject means "throw." What did the coach do when she "rejected" the other play?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She explained it to Priya","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She chose it for the team","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She refused to use it","is_correct":true},{"text":"She wrote it down for later","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She refused to use it$q$, $q$To reject is to "throw back," or turn down, and the coach explains there was no time to try three ideas. Choosing the play is the opposite of rejecting it.$q$, 'draft', 'fc1b71d7-429d-5bf8-8214-cd5d24f0039d')
