  ('69feda29-ab63-594d-8bb0-9c2240cd9b89', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix inter- means "between," and ject means "throw." What does it mean that Jonah "interjected before she could finish"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He tossed the ball between two players during the timeout","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"He broke in with a comment while Priya was still talking","is_correct":true},{"text":"He walked away from the huddle before the plan was set","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He quietly agreed with Priya after she was done talking","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-context"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He broke in with a comment while Priya was still talking$q$, $q$To interject is to "throw between," so Jonah threw his comment into the middle of Priya's speech, before she could finish. Tossing a ball reads the root too literally, since Jonah threw words, not an object.$q$, 'draft', 'fc1b71d7-429d-5bf8-8214-cd5d24f0039d')
