   $q$The prefix contra- means "against," and dict means "say." Why does Priya look at the coach instead of choosing to "contradict" her plan?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She does not want to forget what the coach told the team","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"She does not want to write down the coach's whole plan","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"She does not want to speak against what the coach planned","is_correct":true},{"text":"She does not want to repeat what the coach already said","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She does not want to speak against what the coach planned$q$, $q$Contra plus dict means "say against," so Priya avoids openly going against her coach and waits for the coach to agree. Repeating the plan ignores the prefix contra, which means "against."$q$, 'draft', 'fc1b71d7-429d-5bf8-8214-cd5d24f0039d')
