   $q$The prefix in- can mean "on," and scrip means "write." Which detail from the passage best confirms the meaning of "inscription" suggested by these word parts?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Keiko filled a sketchbook with ideas based on those stories.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"\"She practiced drawing lines that came together at a single point.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-drawing-writing"},{"text":"\"In neat white letters, it read: 'She walked so others could heal.'\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Volunteers helped with the background colors.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"In neat white letters, it read: 'She walked so others could heal.'"$q$, $q$An inscription is writing placed on a surface, and the detail about white letters spelling out a sentence on the wall shows exactly that. Keiko's sketchbook holds ideas, but it is not words written on the wall.$q$, 'draft', 'edb3f6fa-e5cf-5542-ad86-5cf94ab240ca')
