insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7aa7f9ed-f054-5119-8f43-bc577d2cf370', 'rg7-word-parts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Science Fair Surprise$q$, $q$For the seventh-grade science fair, Dmitri Volkov and his partner, Ana Lucia Reyes, wanted to test whether music helps plants grow. They set up two groups of bean plants on the classroom windowsill. One group heard soft piano music for an hour a day. The other group grew in silence.

To keep the test fair, the partners checked conditions every morning. Ana Lucia read a thermometer to make sure both groups stayed at the same temperature. Dmitri measured each plant with a ruler and wrote the numbers in a notebook.

For the music, they placed a small speaker near the first group. They also set a microphone beside the plants to record how loud the music was. The reading showed the sound was gentle. To the silent group across the room, it was inaudible.

Three weeks in, the experiment came to an abrupt stop. A custodian, not knowing about the project, moved all the plants to a dark storage room for a weekend while the windows were cleaned. On Monday, the plants were pale and droopy.

Dmitri was upset, but Ana Lucia saw an opportunity. "We can still report what we learned before the move," she said. "And now we can show what happens when light changes too."

Their teacher, Mr. Osei, agreed that the accident might even be beneficial. Real scientists, he said, often learn the most from surprises. The partners added a new section to their poster, and the judges asked more questions about it than about anything else.$q$, 'draft')
