   $q$What is the author's main claim in this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The school library should stay open until five o'clock on weekdays.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Corbin Middle School has a better library than Halvorsen does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Students should go home and rest after a long school day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"},{"text":"The art club should paint more rooms in the school building.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The school library should stay open until five o'clock on weekdays.$q$, $q$The first paragraph states the claim directly: "The school should keep the library open until five o'clock on weekdays." The idea that students should rest is the opposing view the author answers, not the author's own claim.$q$, 'draft', '7849adca-914b-5525-9f9e-efb71da06e23')
