   $q$Which evidence supports the claim that young players touch the ball more on a small field?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some parents believe players should learn on a real field.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"},{"text":"The league's new uniforms arrived this year in blue and gold.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"A smaller field needs only paint and smaller goals to set up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Players averaged 41 touches per game on a small field and about 18 on a full field.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Players averaged 41 touches per game on a small field and about 18 on a full field.$q$, $q$The coaches' filmed count of touches directly compares the two field sizes. The paint and goals detail is about how easy the change would be, not about touches.$q$, 'draft', '891e9a60-08d6-552e-9a3b-cd23a10a8534')
