   $q$Why is the story about the author's cousin Tomas weak evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It describes a high school player instead of an adult player.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-evidence-type"},{"text":"It contradicts the touch counts that the coaches recorded.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is one person's experience, and many other things could explain his success.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is about a family member, so it must be untrue.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is one person's experience, and many other things could explain his success.$q$, $q$A single example cannot show that small fields caused Tomas to become a strong player, since practice or talent could explain it. The story does not have to be false to be weak; it just proves very little.$q$, 'draft', '891e9a60-08d6-552e-9a3b-cd23a10a8534')
