   $q$Which sentence from the passage adds information that is irrelevant to the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Each one learned to plan a design, measure a wall and work with a team on a deadline.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"\"People have painted on walls for thousands of years, from cave paintings to the frescoes of old palaces.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Painting over graffiti costs the city time and money, so fewer reports also mean lower cleaning costs.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"\"Roads matter, but the mural program costs less than one percent of the city's yearly maintenance budget.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"People have painted on walls for thousands of years, from cave paintings to the frescoes of old palaces."$q$, $q$The long history of wall painting says nothing about whether Ridgeview's program is worth its cost today. The cleaning cost sentence is relevant because it ties fewer graffiti reports to saved money.$q$, 'draft', '1234fd4d-f2ca-5e66-9c39-f11c37341b24')
