   $q$How does the final paragraph connect to the incident at the testing table?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Starting a new design shows the cracked bridge discouraged Tomas from building again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Writing a new design shows Tomas still believes he deserved all the credit for the bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Writing Amara's name beside his own shows the incident taught Tomas to share the work and credit.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Writing Amara's name shows Tomas plans to let her build the next bridge by herself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Writing Amara's name beside his own shows the incident taught Tomas to share the work and credit.$q$, $q$At the start Tomas did not want anyone touching his bridge, but after Amara's catch saved it, he puts her name beside his own before drawing a line. Her name sits "beside his own," so he is sharing the work, not handing it over.$q$, 'draft', '6b2fe5e6-c276-51cd-a2b2-d275918cf54a')
