  ('12eb4bc8-a40e-5903-97ee-da378831596f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The speaker ends by writing "I will come back." How does this line show the effect of the morning's events on the speaker?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker has moved from grumbling to choosing to carry on the family record.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker writes it small because of shame about the low count.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker plans to return only to spend more time with the uncle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The speaker now feels certain that the crabs will soon recover.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker has moved from grumbling to choosing to carry on the family record.$q$, $q$The speaker began by grumbling and questioning the counting, but after seeing the old numbers adds a promise to the notebook itself. The poem gives no sign the speaker expects the crabs to recover; the falling numbers suggest the opposite.$q$, 'draft', '7668d4a1-3bec-54ae-92e0-e86ca1d00d40')
