   $q$In paragraph 5, the reduction in sudden sounds is called "negligible." What does "negligible" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"louder than the original noise","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"careless or poorly done","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"hard for engineers to predict","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"so small that it hardly matters","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$so small that it hardly matters$q$, $q$The text restates negligible as "so small that most listeners barely notice any difference." Sudden sounds are hard to predict, but that is the reason the reduction is small, not the meaning of the word.$q$, 'draft', '1c44f6ff-cb9f-57e6-8e1d-3b3065baea3f')
