   $q$Which sentence best supports the inference that keepers' logbooks are still valuable today?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"In it they recorded the weather, passing ships, and any repairs they made.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"partial-evidence"},{"text":"\"Historians read them to learn about storms, shipwrecks, and daily life along the coast in earlier times.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Keepers were no longer needed, and many stations were left empty.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"Inspectors visited without warning and checked these logbooks, along with the shine on every piece of metal.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-period"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Historians read them to learn about storms, shipwrecks, and daily life along the coast in earlier times."$q$, $q$Only the sentence about historians shows people using the logbooks now. The sentence about what keepers recorded tells what is in the logbooks but not that anyone uses them today.$q$, 'draft', '71b51725-6704-547c-8957-ff13f000b1a2')
