   $q$According to the passage, what does the microphone on the outside of each ear cup do?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It makes the listener's music louder than the noise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It creates a new sound wave that is a mirror image.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-steps"},{"text":"It blocks outside sound with a layer of thick padding.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"It listens to the sounds around the person wearing them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It listens to the sounds around the person wearing them.$q$, $q$The passage says the microphone "listens to the sound around you." The chip, not the microphone, creates the mirror-image wave.$q$, 'draft', '5926b490-2222-522a-9061-0bf4c852108e')
