   $q$Based on the passage, what can be inferred about a teenage athlete who often stays up late looking at a screen?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The athlete no longer needs active recovery after games.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The athlete may recover from training more slowly than possible.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The athlete will become overtrained within a few days.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"The screen itself causes tiny tears in the muscle fibers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The athlete may recover from training more slowly than possible.$q$, $q$The passage says sleep helps "rebuild muscle and bone" and that screens at night cut into teenagers' sleep, so recovery may suffer. Nothing in the text says this leads to overtraining within days.$q$, 'draft', 'c4cb6e84-5cb9-5608-acfd-145dea8d4e7f')
