   $q$Which detail best supports the inference that the team wanted the restored mural to last a long time?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They talked with neighbors who remembered the mural.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"They chose paints made to resist fading in sunlight.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They found faint red paint at the far left edge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"They spent a total of three months on the work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They chose paints made to resist fading in sunlight.$q$, $q$Paint that resists fading protects the mural from the same sun that damaged it before. Talking with neighbors helped the team learn how it once looked, not make it last.$q$, 'draft', '907d3804-cc16-5957-b6c5-115b7eb8ad05')
